v 3
d gepwreg. Percentile weights regression: effects at a quantile of the outcome
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar
d Universite Laval and Partnership for Economic Policy (PEP)
d Support: aabd@ecn.ulaval.ca
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260919
d
d Description:
d gepwreg estimates the effect of the covariates on an outcome for the
d units located at a target quantile of the outcome, at the initial
d quantile (the outcome before the contribution of the covariates), or
d along the rank of an observed covariate, with the percentile weights of
d Araar (2016).  Version 1.4 estimates the effect at a quantile of the
d outcome by a two-step estimator (unit-level effects from a heterogeneity
d model -- conditional quantile regression, or interactions with observed
d variables -- averaged with the percentile weights), with analytical
d standard errors by linearisation, Taylor linearisation under a complex
d survey design declared by svyset, and a bootstrap that re-runs the whole
d procedure.  The bandwidth of every estimator is the MSE-optimal plug-in
d of Araar (2026); silverman and band() override it.  The kernel-weighted
d regression on outcome-ranked units of the
d earlier versions is kept as a descriptive option (rankdep); see the help
d file and Araar (2026, doi:10.5281/zenodo.22845708).
d With het(varlist), merr corrects step 1 for classical measurement error
d in the heterogeneity variables: one error variance per variable,
d identified from the third moments of the step-1 residual, applied only
d where it is identified and where the data support it.
d gepwreg_setable, a post-estimation command, compares the standard
d errors; a dialog box is included.
d
d bkf98I.dta, retrieved by net get, is the Burkina Faso 1998 household
d survey extract used in the paper and in the help file examples.
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
f gepwreg.ado
f gepwreg_setable.ado
f gepwreg.sthlp
f gepwreg.dlg
f bkf98I.dta
